++## Intent
++
++**Problem:** v2's build layer is free (unlimited routers/pipes), so only the react layer ever asks anything of the player — the ratified diagnosis (mechanics-quinn record). The user adopted 7 rulings building "The Box, capped per era, refilled by tempo": typed pieces (1G/40G/100G routers, standard/fiber spools) against era caps; draws drain spools 1/tile; placements spend a piece; promotion is a swap (higher spent, lower returns); teardown refunds everything; refill dots restore-to-cap on a known clock spine accelerated by deliveries (floor/ceiling bounded); era advance raises caps + shifts spool mix. Eras 1–2 fat and calm (authored brushes); Era 3 demand outruns restore.
++
++**Approach:** A `core/box.odin` material authority behind a `box_enabled` run-setup flag (the growth/health/advance-gate pattern): `box_apply_edit` wraps the existing validate-then-apply path with material validate + charge/refund; a dot clock lives in `core.step` beside `era_step`; caps/cadences are data (eras.json rows, balance.json, pipe_tiers spool tags); the app gates the tray, surfaces refusals, and adds ONE minimal HUD line. Golden-stability: box-off runs stay byte-identical (delegate path); box numbers fold catalog_hash → deliberate re-bless, disclosed. No new commands, LOG_VERSION stays 6.
++
++## Boundaries & Constraints
++
++**Always:**
++- The 7 record rulings are USER rulings — implement, never re-design. Rollback dials are tuning surfaces, not reversals.
++- FORGE #2: zero player arithmetic — counts small, prices integer, HUD glanceable.
++- No-soft-lock: the clock FLOOR is absolute ("always available"); full teardown refund + piece returns hold at every tuning. Never gate the floor on performance.
++- Integer-only sim (ODN-10), no maps in core (ODN-10), events not callbacks (ODN-14), numbers single-source in data/*.json (ODN-5, fail-fast validated).
++- Golden-stability idiom: box-off = byte-identical delegate; box sections serialize absent-when-disabled; new event tags append only.
++- Tune numbers ONLY against sim runs; final numbers + run evidence live in the PR body.
++
++**Ask First:**
++- Any conflict between a ruling and something found in code (era table, tier ladder, ports) — HALT, flag to Gru (user amends via the mechanics-quinn record; never minion initiative).
++- If the diff approaches ~20k lines, the MEGA-DIFF protocol applies — say so before opening the PR.
++
++**Never:**
++- No new Command kinds; no LOG_VERSION bump; no save/migration system (v2 dev build: saves disposable — flag the choice in the PR).
++- No render/look rework beyond the minimal HUD line + tray count labels (congestion-read-a1 owns render; its palcheck fixtures are off-limits). No popups/tutorials — economy teaches by consequence.
++- No score-milestone refills (ruling 5's clock+ledger is the refill spine), no banking (restore clamps at cap; refunds are unclamped — full refund is an explicit ruling), no cross-spool conversion.
++
++## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
++
++| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
++|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
++| Draw drains spool | box-on; draw span S, standard tier | spool -S; pipe applies; logged | N/A |
++| Spool short | spool stock < span | whole draw rejected (atomic, no partial) | `.Box_Spool_Exhausted` toast; nothing logged |
++| Place held tier | box-on; piece stock > 0 | piece -1; router applies | N/A |
++| Place unheld tier | stock 0 (e.g. router_mid pre-era-3) | rejected | `.Box_Piece_Exhausted`; tray shows it disabled |
++| Modernize (resplice) | standard→mid, span S | fiber -S, standard +S (matching spools) | `.Box_Spool_Exhausted` if fiber short |
++| Demolish pipe/router | any live entity | FULL refund: tiles → matching spool, router piece → stock (batch = atomic refund) | N/A |
++| Era advance | gate fires era N | caps = era N row; ALL types restored to cap (never past) | N/A |
++| Dot fires | tick ≥ next_dot_tick | restore-to-cap; BOX_DOT event; baseline reset; next scheduled | N/A |
++| Acceleration | D deliveries since last dot | next interval = clamp(base − accel·D, floor, base) | crisis (0 deliveries) → interval rides at base — spine is the worst case |
++| Box-off run | box_enabled false | byte-identical to pre-change sim (delegate) | legacy goldens shift only by catalog_hash fold |
++
