+## Tasks & Acceptance
+
+**Execution (staged commits, L1→L5, one PR):**
+- [ ] `data/pipe_tiers.json`, `data/eras.json`, `data/balance.json` + `core/catalog.odin` -- L1 data spine: spool tags, per-era box cap rows, dot clock block; fail-fast load + validation -- numbers single-source, era advance raises caps by data alone.
+- [ ] `core/types.odin`, `core/box.odin` -- L1: Box_State, box_enable/restore-to-cap (clamp), full-refund accounting, pieces/spools parallel arrays -- The Box + The Cap (rulings 2+3+6 stock model).
+- [ ] `core/box.odin`, `core/step.odin`, `core/topology.odin` (comments only) -- L2: box_apply_edit material grammar — place costs held piece (ruling 4), draw drains matching spool 1/tile, modernize = spool swap, demolish = full refund; new Edit_Error values -- placement + promotion grammar, ZERO new commands.
+- [ ] `core/box.odin`, `core/step.odin`, `core/era.odin`, `core/serialize.odin`, `core/types.odin` -- L3: dot clock spine + delivery acceleration clamped [floor, base]; BOX_DOT tag 17; era-advance restore hook; box serialization absent-when-disabled -- ruling 5; the floor is the no-soft-lock guarantee.
+- [ ] `data/*.json` (era rows), `core/catalog.odin` -- L4: era 1–2 fat caps (felt-not-counted), era 3 mix shift + squeeze staging -- ruling 7 shape; values finalized by L5.
+- [ ] `app/input/input.odin`, `app/input/exec.odin`, `app/qos_panel.odin`, `app/main.odin`, `app/render/tray.odin` -- L4b: app wiring — state ref, box entry path, reject strings, tray counts, ONE HUD line -- minimal glanceable layer only.
+- [ ] `harness/demo.odin`, `harness/run.odin` -- box_on demo flag + a `box_spine` demo (draw→refuse→dot→demolish→advance→resplice arc) -- golden coverage of the box arc.
+- [ ] `core/box_test.odin` (NEW) -- L5 gates: refusal matrix, dot/acceleration bounds, era restore, refund overflow, replay determinism (box-on record→replay byte-identical); ECONOMY GATES THAT CAN FAIL: brush-frequency + first-no timing with mutation legs (caps deleted → RED; floor mutated to 0 → RED) + a no-soft-lock pin (floor intact ⇒ teardown-refund always affords a redraw) -- record open question 8, mandatory.
+- [ ] `core/determinism_test.odin`, `core/catalog_test.odin` -- mirror the new Era_Row/catalog fields in fixtures -- the 6.3 collapse lesson.
+- [ ] `harness/main.odin`, `harness/econ.odin` (NEW), `core/stats.odin` -- econ-check verb + stats box columns; run the 4 scenarios; tune era rows/clock numbers against runs -- L5 calibration, evidence into the PR body; prove crisis-stall degrades to the base spine, never past the floor (record Q7).
+- [ ] `goldens/` -- re-bless (harness save); run fold-check to prove legacy deltas are the catalog_hash fold alone; disclose inventory in PR -- harness doctrine.
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given a box-off legacy golden run, when re-run post-change, then T1 hashes are byte-identical modulo the catalog_hash fold (fold-check proves it) and LOG_VERSION is still 6.
+- Given a box-on recorded run, when replayed from its action log, then per-tick hashes are byte-identical (E10).
+- Given era-2 greedy play under the tuned numbers, when the sim runs, then the first refusal lands on a greedy-but-SAFE player with zero pressure and each brush self-resolves as a dot lands (brush-frequency + first-no gates GREEN).
+- Given the caps or floor are mutated away in a fixture, then the corresponding gate turns RED (mutation-leg proof the gates can fail).
+- Given a crisis stalls deliveries, when dots continue, then the interval degrades to the base spine and never exceeds it; teardown+refund affords a rebuild (no-soft-lock pin GREEN).
+- Given era advance fires, then every type restores to the new era's cap exactly (never past; refunds above cap are never clamped).
+- Given the app with box on, when the player opens the tray, then held tiers show counts, empty tiers are visibly disabled, and the HUD shows pieces + next-dot in ONE glanceable line (no arithmetic).
+
+## Spec Change Log
+
+- **r1 (step-04 review swarm, 2026-08-28):** the review round surfaced (a) Code Map drift — the tray work lives in `app/main.odin` (`draw_tray`), not `app/render/tray.odin` (which is geometry-only); `Box_State.spools` (not spool_stock); the serialized box section also carries `dot_interval` (the HUD progress denominator); (b) two review-driven behavior amendments inside the non-frozen implementation space: same-spool resplices (mid→wide) price NET-ZERO and never refuse on a short spool (a net-free upgrade refusing would be a false "no"), and the era box caps are cross-checked at load against the unlock rosters (a cap on a not-yet-introduced tier/spool is dead stock — rejected at load; era-2's fiber grant moved to era 3 accordingly). KEEP instructions: the box-off golden-stability delegate path (byte-identical legacy runs), the `Box_Charge_Snapshot` pre-apply pricing pattern (validate snapshots, charge prices — post-apply reads are the hazard class), the refusal-feedback requirement (every material refusal surfaces on the reject toast), and the era-3 two-sided bind reading (tile refusals OR the piece wall — the record's "every draw is material off the board").
+
+## Design Notes
+
+- Promotion needs NO new verb: router "swap" = demolish (piece returns) + place higher tier (piece spent) — lifetime cost equals place-big-first, exactly ruling 4's contract. Pipe modernize (Cmd_Set_Pipe_Tier) resplices spools: new tier's tiles drain the matching spool, old tier's tiles refund theirs.
+- Spool identity is era-invariant tech class (data on pipe_tiers), caps are era-relative (data on era rows) — era advance "shifts spool mix" without code.
+- Initial stock = start-era restore-to-cap at box_enable (run setup, before tick 1 — not a logged event; deterministic).
+- Acceleration is a countdown-anchored schedule: next_dot_tick moves closer only at dot fire time... it is computed AT the previous dot (clamp there), so the HUD's next-dot progress is a pure read of serialized state. Deliveries mid-interval do NOT reschedule — they set the NEXT interval (known worst case preserved: the player can always read when the dot lands).
+- Re-bless inventory: ALL .t1 manifests shift via the catalog_hash fold (balance/eras/pipe_tiers content changed); box demos add new entries; T2 pixels unchanged except any capture that frames the new HUD line (box-off demos never draw it). Disclose per-file in the PR.
+- Numbers below are L1 staging starts, replaced by L5 sim-tuned values (recorded in the PR): era1 {basic:6, std:240, fiber:0}, era2 {basic:8, std:320, fiber:0}, era3 {basic:8, mid:3, high:2, std:320, fiber:360}; clock base 2400 ticks, floor 600, accel 1 tick/delivery.
